DESCRIPTION:Book Club\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nStart your Wednesday with a si
 de of storytelling. The MTPL Book Discussion Group meets the 2nd Wednesday
  of each month at 10am to explore new worlds together. It’s more than ju
 st a book club-- it’s your monthly morning retreat for thoughtful talk a
 nd local connection!Please register for each meeting\, as it allows the li
 brary to update you if there are any changes to a meeting due to weather d
 elays\, closures\, or other circumstances.January 13: Age of Innocence by 
 Edith WhartonFebruary 10: Becoming Madam Secretary by Stephanie DrayMarch 
 10: Remarkably Bright Creatures by Shelby Van PeltApril 14: My Ántonia by
  Willa CatherMay 12: Land by Maggie O’FarrellJune 9: American Ramble by 
 Neil King Jr.July 14: The God of the Woods by Liz MooreAugust 11: American
  Way of Killing by Malcolm GladwellSeptember 8: John of John by Douglas St
 uartOctober 13: A Woman I Know by Mary HaverstickNovember 10: Theo of Gold
 en by Allen LeviDecember 8: How to Read a Book by Monica Wood
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center A
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/mtpl-book-discussion-gro
 up-213769
