SUMMARY:Creating My Wellness Plan
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270120T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270120T190000
UID:c849cd1125c5cd5df5bb839da0dc4d04@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Discussion\, Teens\n\nTeens are invited on a journey to create
  a personalized Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP). WRAP is an evidence-
 based\, interactive\, psycho-educational course where teens will explore s
 tressors\, early warning signs\, crisis planning and developing their own 
 wellness toolbox. This six-week program will be led by Licensed Clinical S
 ocial Worker\, Janae Allgire and Master's Level Social Worker\, Ashlee Rin
 eer. Session One: Intro to WrapSession Two: Wellness ToolboxSession Three:
  My Daily PlanSession Four: StressorsSession Five: Early Warning Signs & W
 hen Things Break DownSession Six: Crisis & Post-CrisisParticipants who att
 end at least four out of the six sessions will receive a Visa gift card wo
 rth $45. Space is limited · Registration is requiredAges 14-18This series
  is made possible by the LGBTQ+ Giving Circle & All Seasons Wellness LLC.
LOCATION:Lancaster\, LPL Meeting and Media Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/creating-my-wellness-pla
 n-212919
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
